  "method": "For each of the 24 compare spots, pitch_fit.probe() was run at column 0.5 on the level (pitch-zeroed) render captured in the first run (renders-pitch0-<apt>/) and again on the same spot's render from the independent repeat run (renders-pitch0-repeat-<apt>/, a fresh page load -- new bake, new environment capture). Each probe returns up to 8 candidate horizontal-edge rows with their gradient strength. Candidate rows from the two runs were greedy-matched by position (within 10% of frame height), and among the matched pairs the one with the highest combined strength was taken as 'the strongest shared row' for that spot -- the same physical landmark caught by both captures, not necessarily the single strongest candidate in either probe alone. row_diff_frac is |row1 - row2| / (height - 1). bandRows is the maximum row_diff_frac across all 24 spots (a deliberately conservative single figure, not a mean). bandDegrees converts bandRows to a pitch-degree equivalent at the legacy 72 degree vertical FOV by numerically inverting pitch_fit.remap_rows itself (fed an identity-ramp profile so its output array IS the clipped render-row-index mapping, bisected at the frame's center column) -- not a hand-derived trig simplification, per the task brief.",
